{"nodes": [{"id": "title", "type": "text", "text": "Module 17 — Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery\nBC vs DR → BIA → RTO vs RPO → five activities → BCP/DRP/NDRP → standards", "x": -1200, "y": -3600, "width": 2400, "height": 70, "color": "5"}, {"id": "b1", "type": "text", "text": "LO01 · BC vs DR  (pp4-9)\n\nBC = continuity of CRITICAL FUNCTIONS\nduring + after disaster; ISO: delivery\nat ACCEPTABLE PREDEFINED LEVELS\nBUSINESS-CENTRIC (operations over IT)\n\n5 OBJECTIVES\n  maintain continuity · PROTECT REPUTATION\n  · preparedness · COMPLIANCE benefits ·\n  mitigate risks + financial losses\n\nBCM (p7) — owns recovery, crisis,\nincident, emergency, contingency mgmt\n  goals: resilience · disaster response ·\n  minimise loss · reviews + mock drills\n  CM (brand/revenue) · EMERGENCY MGMT =\n  safeguard PEOPLE from harm · DR element =\n  restore hardware/IT/comms\n\nDR (p9) = ABILITY TO RESTORE DATA +\nAPPLICATIONS; DATA-CENTRIC (IT over\nbusiness)\n  objectives: reduce DOWNTIME · reduce\n  LOSSES · recover HW-damaged data", "x": -2400, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b2", "type": "text", "text": "LO01 · BIA + RTO vs RPO  (pp10-14)\n\nBIA = SYSTEMATIC PROCESS on\ninterruption effects to critical ops\n  ascertains recovery TIME + REQUIREMENTS\n  planning + exploratory components\n  ends in a REPORT (feeds DRP + BCP)\n  ANALYSIS TOOL ONLY — implements nothing\n  in the BCP\n\nPRINTED PHASES (no fixed guidelines)\n  1 Initiation (scope, team)\n  2 Acquisition (interviews, QUESTIONNAIRE\n    surveys)\n  3 Analysis (prioritised process list)\n  5 Presentation to management\n  ✗ NO PHASE 4 IN THE SOURCE\n\nRTO (p13) = MAX TOLERABLE DOWN TIME\n  process-owner set; eg 45 min / 3 h / 96 h\nRPO (p14) = MAX DATA-LOSS TIME FRAME\n  acceptable loss; drives BC/DR/HA goals\n\n  ✗ RTO≠data-loss, RPO≠down-time", "x": -1740, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b3", "type": "text", "text": "LO02 · FIVE ACTIVITIES  (pp15-18)\n\n1 PREVENTION\n  stop the hazard harming the org\n  eg SPENDING RESTRICTIONS to DRP/BCP items\n  controls deny access, no availability loss\n\n2 RESPONSE\n  needs assessment post-disaster\n  EVACUATE, SHUT DOWN systems\n  notifications · BCT ACTIVATION · briefing\n\n3 RESUMPTION\n  RECOMMENCEMENT at primary OR alternate\n  FIRST DECISION: primary vs alternate\n  large-scale → EMERGENCY OPS CENTER\n\n4 RECOVERY\n  resume services on critical apps\n  STABLE + USABLE condition\n\n5 RESTORATION\n  repair PRIMARY site or build new;\n  migrate back from recovery site\n  PHYSICAL DAMAGE ONLY; ops team SPLITS IN\n  TWO; both phases often SIMULTANEOUS", "x": -1080, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b4", "type": "text", "text": "LO03 · BCP + DRP + NDRP  (pp19-26)\n\nBCP = COMPREHENSIVE DOCUMENT for\nresilience UNDER ADVERSE CONDITIONS\n  7 GOALS (p20)\n    analyse risks/losses · ENABLE RISK MGMT\n    · safety/health/welfare · minimise\n    infra damage · PRE-DISASTER conditions\n    · VITAL DOCUMENTS (phones, vendors)\n    · TRAINING + pre-defined comms\n\nDRP = for SPECIFIC DEPARTMENTS (p22)\n  4 GOALS: REDUCE overall risk (assess\n    vulns first) · senior-mgmt concerns ·\n    REGULATORY COMPLIANCE · RAPID response\n\nNDRP (p23) = AVAILABILITY, INTEGRITY,\nRESILIENCE of NET infrastructure\n  back up ALL network services\n  BC standards · TEST OFTEN · prioritise\n  objectives · ZERO TRUST architecture\n\nELEMENTS\n  good BCP: risk assessment + BIA ·\n  response planning · ROLES · comms ·\n  testing + training\n  good DRP: RTO · RPO · COMMS PLAN (+backup\n  channels) · client protocols · ASSET\n  INVENTORY · employee safety", "x": -420, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b5", "type": "text", "text": "LO04 · STANDARDS  (pp27-36)\n\nISO 22301:2019 — BCMS REQUIREMENTS\n  protect/reduce/prepare/respond/recover;\n  GENERIC, any org or part\nISO 22313:2012 — GUIDES 22301\n  good international practice; NO UNIFORMITY\n  implied\nISO/IEC 27031:2011 — ICT READINESS (IRBC)\n  any org, any size\nFINRA 4370 — written BCP per member;\n  CUSTOMISED (backup + alt comms + alt\n  sites); PRINCIPAL approves, ANNUAL review;\n  WRITTEN DISCLOSURE; TWO contacts (one\n  senior principal); MISSION-CRITICAL =\n  accurate transaction processing + logs\nASIS ORM.1 (as printed) — integrated\n  risk approach; ASIS = volunteer nonprofit,\n  NO enforcement power\n  www.asisonline.org\nMORE TITLES (pp34-35)\n  22320:2018 (COMMAND + CONTROL) · 31000 ·\n  Guide 73 (vocabulary) · 31010 ·\n  TS 22317 (BIA) · NFPA 1600 · SP 800-34\n\n  ✗ FINRA URL garbled → not recorded", "x": 240, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "pat", "type": "text", "text": "THE MODULE'S FOUR TRAPS\n\n1 · BC vs DR AXIS\n  business-centric vs data-centric — every\n  which-plan item turns on it\n2 · RTO vs RPO\n  down-time vs data-lost; printed twice with\n  different wording (pp13-14, p26)\n3 · THE MISSING PHASE\n  BIA prints 1, 2, 3, 5 — no Phase 4;\n  any content for it is invented\n4 · REQUIREMENTS vs GUIDANCE\n  22301 states, 22313 guides; ASIS enforces\n  nothing; FINRA wants TWO contacts;\n  restoration = PRIMARY site only", "x": -2400, "y": -2620, "width": 2040, "height": 520, "color": "6"}], "edges": [{"id": "e1", "fromNode": "b1", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b2", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e2", "fromNode": "b2", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b3", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e3", "fromNode": "b3", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b4", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e4", "fromNode": "b4", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b5", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e5", "fromNode": "b5", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "pat", "toSide": "top"}]}